---
// The mini-briefing flow, first iteration, 2026-08-13.
//
// Daniel: "pill --> card/side panel --> site flow. can the card be vatiable
// size too? and can a user scroll and or click while is chugging in the bg."
// Plus four decisions taken today: the in-page card is the default surface,
// accuracy wins over speed on the first output, cost varies by what triggered
// the run, and the card shrinks to a marker while it works.
//
// Every number here is measured, not estimated. The thinking-budget table is
// scripts/bench-outline.ts run three times over three articles, nine runs per
// setting. The timings and costs are scripts/run-mini.ts on 13 August 2026.
//
// This is an iteration to be refined, not a shipped design. Noindex, no ads.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const CLAIM = 'Nuclear reactors operate approximately 90 per cent of the time.';

// scripts/bench-outline.ts, 9 runs per budget across 3 articles.
const BENCH = [
  { budget: '0',    secs: 2.4, claims: 2.7, check: 1.3, quality: 0.72, cost: '$0.00071', chosen: false },
  { budget: '512',  secs: 4.7, claims: 3.0, check: 1.7, quality: 0.89, cost: '$0.00079', chosen: true  },
  { budget: '2048', secs: 8.0, claims: 3.3, check: 1.8, quality: 0.82, cost: '$0.00088', chosen: false },
  { budget: '8192', secs: 9.4, claims: 3.3, check: 1.7, quality: 0.75, cost: '$0.00085', chosen: false },
];
const MAXQ = 1.0;
---

<Base title="Mini-briefing flow (labs) - The Whetstone" noAds={true}>
  <Fragment slot="head"><meta name="robots" content="noindex" /></Fragment>

  <div class="fl">
    <p class="kicker">The Whetstone · labs · 13 August 2026 · iteration 1</p>
    <h1>Pill, card, site</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One run, start to finish, at the sizes each step actually takes. Four decisions are built in:
      the card is the default surface, the first output takes as long as it needs to be right, cost
      follows what triggered the run, and the card gets out of the way while it works.
    </p>

    <div class="facts">
      <div><b>4.7s</b><span>outline on screen</span></div>
      <div><b>35s</b><span>fully sourced</span></div>
      <div><b>$0.042</b><span>from a selection</span></div>
      <div><b>$0.081</b><span>from a whole article</span></div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============================================================ flow -->
    <p class="sizetag">The flow</p>
    <h2>1 · You select a sentence</h2>
    <p class="note">
      The pill is the trigger because it arrives at the moment you are already interested, without
      you having gone looking for it. Selecting also tells the tool <em>which</em> claim you care
      about, so it searches once instead of twice.
    </p>

    <div class="win">
      <div class="chrome">
        <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="addr">news.example.com/nuclear-costings</span><span class="ico">W</span>
      </div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <div class="page">
          <p class="arttitle">Australia should build nuclear power</p>
          <div class="rule w90"></div>
          <p class="selected">reactors run about 90 per cent of the time, far above what wind and solar manage</p>
          <div class="rule w85"></div><div class="rule w95"></div><div class="rule w70"></div>
          <div class="rule w90"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pill">Check this claim</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec">
      <div><b>Costs</b>Nothing until pressed. No pixels before you select.</div>
      <div><b>Scopes it</b>One claim, not four. Half the bill, half the wait.</div>
      <div><b>Then</b>The card opens where you are. The panel does not.</div>
    </div>

    <h2>2 · The card works while you read</h2>
    <p class="note">
      This is the answer to whether you can scroll and click while it runs. You can. The work happens
      in the extension's background, not in the page, so nothing you do to the page touches it. The
      card shrinks itself to a marker so it is not sitting in your eye-line for thirty seconds.
    </p>

    <div class="states">
      <div class="state">
        <p class="stname">While working <span class="sh">44px</span></p>
        <div class="cardbox h44">
          <div class="marker">
            <span class="mtitle">THE WHETSTONE</span>
            <span class="mprog">checking 1 claim</span>
            <span class="mtick">·</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="stwhy">Shrinks by itself. Scroll, click, open a tab: none of it interrupts the run.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="state">
        <p class="stname">Outline, 4.7s <span class="sh">280px</span></p>
        <div class="cardbox h280">
          <div class="cardin">
            <p class="phead">THE WHETSTONE <span class="clock">4.7s</span> <span class="x">×</span></p>
            <p class="prests">CHECKING</p>
            <p class="pclaim">{CLAIM}</p>
            <p class="prests">IF IT IS FALSE</p>
            <p class="pconc">The cost advantage over renewables shrinks or disappears.</p>
            <p class="pwait">· looking for who disputes it</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="stwhy">Something to read at 4.7 seconds. Stands up alone even if the rest returns nothing.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="state">
        <p class="stname">Sourced, 35s <span class="sh">430px</span></p>
        <div class="cardbox h430">
          <div class="cardin">
            <p class="phead">THE WHETSTONE <span class="clock">35s</span> <span class="x">×</span></p>
            <p class="prests">{CLAIM}</p>
            <p class="stance contests">CONTESTS<span class="who">World Nuclear Association</span></p>
            <p class="quote">“In 2023 the global average capacity factor was 81.5%, up from 80.4% in 2022”</p>
            <p class="stance supports">SUPPORTS<span class="who">Duke Energy</span></p>
            <p class="quote">“the average nuclear plant generates electricity, more than 90 percent of the time”</p>
            <p class="handoff">Open in full →</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="stwhy">Disagreement first. This is the ceiling: one more claim would not fit a laptop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note tight">
      <b>Why it shrinks rather than hides.</b> Hidden means forgotten, and a run you forgot about is
      money spent for nothing. The marker is small enough to ignore and present enough to remember.
      Pressing it brings the card back at any point.
    </p>

    <h2>3 · The site takes over when the card runs out of room</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Press <em>Open in full</em> and the finished briefing goes to the site and opens in a tab. The
      answer travels, not the question: nothing is analysed twice and you are not charged twice. The
      card stays where it is, so closing the tab loses nothing.
    </p>

    <div class="win mid">
      <div class="chrome">
        <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="addr">thewhetstone.review/m/k3f9qp2x</span>
      </div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <div class="hosted">
          <p class="hkick">THE WHETSTONE · MINI-BRIEFING · 13 AUGUST 2026</p>
          <p class="htitle">Do reactors run 90 per cent of the time?</p>
          <p class="hconc">
            The figure holds for the United States fleet and does not hold as a global average. Which
            one an argument needs depends on what it is comparing.
          </p>
          <div class="hgrid">
            <div>
              <p class="prests">CONTESTS</p>
              <p class="stance contests">World Nuclear Association<span class="who">world-nuclear.org</span></p>
              <p class="quote">“In 2023 the global average capacity factor was 81.5%, up from 80.4% in 2022, continuing the trend of high global capacity factors seen since 2000.”</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="prests">SUPPORTS</p>
              <p class="stance supports">Duke Energy<span class="who">duke-energy.com</span></p>
              <p class="quote">“the average nuclear plant generates electricity, more than 90 percent of the time”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="hfoot">Every quote checked against the page it came from. Three were dropped for being about a different quantity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec">
      <div><b>Costs</b>Nothing extra. It sends the answer, not the question.</div>
      <div><b>Private</b>The briefing travels. The article you were reading does not.</div>
      <div><b>Unlocks</b>A link you can send to somebody with nothing installed.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================================================== preference -->
    <p class="sizetag">Preference</p>
    <h2>4 · Where it appears, if you want it somewhere else</h2>
    <p class="note">
      The card is the default because it is the only surface that survives you reading the article.
      The other two stay available for people who want them, and the setting is one screen, not a
      section of settings.
    </p>

    <div class="prefwrap">
      <div class="prefs">
        <p class="pgroup">SHOW BRIEFINGS</p>
        <label class="opt on"><span class="radio"></span><b>In the page</b><span>Bottom right, out of the column. Default.</span></label>
        <label class="opt"><span class="radio"></span><b>Side panel</b><span>Roomier. Takes 300px of the window all session.</span></label>
        <label class="opt"><span class="radio"></span><b>Toolbar popup</b><span>Closes when you click back on the article.</span></label>

        <p class="pgroup">WHILE IT IS WORKING</p>
        <label class="opt on"><span class="radio"></span><b>Shrink to a marker</b><span>Default.</span></label>
        <label class="opt"><span class="radio"></span><b>Stay open</b><span></span></label>
        <label class="opt"><span class="radio"></span><b>Hide, mark the toolbar icon</b><span></span></label>
      </div>
      <div class="prefnote">
        <p><b>Why the popup is offered at all.</b> It cannot hold a thirty-five second reveal, because
          clicking back on the article closes it. But some people want briefings kept out of the page
          entirely, and telling them no would be worse than letting them find out.</p>
        <p><b>What this displaces.</b> The side panel stops being the front door. It is still there,
          still works, and is no longer the thing you have to open before anything happens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ========================================================== curve -->
    <p class="sizetag">Measured</p>
    <h2>5 · What a longer wait actually buys</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Stage one is the only wait anybody feels: everything after it happens while there is already
      something on screen. So it is the one place where seconds are worth trading for accuracy. Nine
      runs per setting, three articles. Quality is scored mechanically, by whether a claim names
      somebody, carries a figure with a unit, and avoids leaning on “this” or “the study”.
    </p>

    <div class="chart">
      <div class="crow head">
        <div class="cbud"></div><div class="cbar">quality per claim</div>
        <div class="csec">wait</div><div class="ccost">cost</div><div class="cmark"></div>
      </div>
      {BENCH.map((b) => (
        <div class={b.chosen ? 'crow chosen' : 'crow'}>
          <div class="cbud">{b.budget}<span>thinking</span></div>
          <div class="cbar">
            <div class="cfill" style={`width:${(b.quality / MAXQ) * 100}%`}></div>
            <span class="cval">{b.quality.toFixed(2)}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="csec">{b.secs.toFixed(1)}s</div>
          <div class="ccost">{b.cost}</div>
          <div class="cmark">{b.chosen ? 'CHOSEN' : ''}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="note tight">
      <b>The finding.</b> Yes, a longer wait buys accuracy, and the useful range is narrow. Going from
      no thinking to 512 tokens costs 2.3 seconds and is the single biggest jump. Past that, the model
      writes <em>more</em> claims and the extra ones are vaguer, so quality per claim falls while the
      wait keeps rising. Since each claim researched is a real search downstream, padding the list
      costs money later.
    </p>
    <p class="note tight">
      <b>Cost never decides here.</b> The whole range is $0.0007 to $0.0009, about one per cent of a
      run. Search is 91 per cent of the bill, and search happens after the reader is already reading.
      The only currency at stage one is seconds.
    </p>

    <table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th>Triggered by</th><th>Claims researched</th><th>Cost</th><th>Fully sourced</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>A sentence you selected</td><td>1, the one you pointed at</td><td>$0.042</td><td>about 20s</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A whole article</td><td>2, so it can show more than one weak point</td><td>$0.081</td><td>about 35s</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="note blocker">
      <b>Still blocking.</b> Nothing in the extension streams: every path is one message and one
      reply, so there is no way to send an outline now and premises later. Until that exists, every
      state above is a picture of a thing that cannot happen yet. It is the first build, and it is
      small: a long-lived connection, or a job written to storage that the card reads as it updates.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .fl {
    --pp:#F3F4F1; --ss:#FBFBF9; --ii:#24272B; --is:#121417; --mm:#5C6167; --hh:#D7D9D3;
    --ox:#8C4A2F; --db:#345D7E;
    --sf: 'Besley Variable', Georgia, serif;
    --mo: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    max-width: 62rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 20px 80px;
    font-family: var(--sf); color: var(--ii); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .fl h1 { font-size: 34px; color: var(--is); font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 10px; line-height: 1.15; }
  .fl h2 { font-size: 20px; color: var(--is); font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 6px; line-height: 1.25; }
  .fl .kicker, .fl .sizetag { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mm); margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .fl .sizetag { margin: 54px 0 10px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); }
  .fl .lede { font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 24px; max-width: 42rem; }
  .fl .note { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 42rem; }
  .fl .note.tight { margin-top: 18px; }
  .fl .blocker { margin-top: 30px; padding: 16px 18px; background: var(--pp); border-left: 3px solid var(--is); max-width: none; }
  .fl em { font-style: italic; }

  .fl .facts { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 16px 0 4px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hh); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .fl .facts div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .fl .facts b { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .facts span { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 13px; color: var(--mm); }

  /* browser frame, same drawing language as the formats page */
  .fl .win { border: 1px solid var(--hh); border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.06); }
  .fl .chrome { background: #E8E9E5; padding: 7px 10px; display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hh); }
  .fl .dot { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: #C9CBC5; display: inline-block; }
  .fl .addr { flex: 1; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--hh); border-radius: 11px; padding: 2px 10px; font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 11px; color: var(--mm); margin-left: 6px; }
  .fl .ico { width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 3px; background: #D2D4CE; color: var(--mm); font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 11px; display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .fl .viewport { height: 260px; display: flex; position: relative; background: #fff; overflow: hidden; }
  .fl .win.mid .viewport { height: 400px; }
  .fl .page { flex: 1; padding: 20px 30px; }
  .fl .arttitle { font-size: 17px; color: var(--is); margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.25; }
  .fl .rule { height: 7px; background: #EDEEEA; border-radius: 2px; margin-bottom: 9px; }
  .fl .w70 { width: 70%; } .fl .w85 { width: 85%; } .fl .w90 { width: 90%; } .fl .w95 { width: 95%; }
  .fl .selected { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; background: #E4E9EE; color: var(--is); margin: 0 0 9px; padding: 3px 4px; border-radius: 2px; }
  .fl .pill { position: absolute; left: 34px; top: 92px; background: var(--is); color: #fff; font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 11px; padding: 5px 11px; border-radius: 13px; }

  /* the card, at its three real heights */
  .fl .states { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 22px; align-items: start; }
  .fl .stname { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--is); margin: 0 0 7px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
  .fl .sh { color: var(--mm); }
  .fl .cardbox { background: var(--ss); border: 1px solid var(--hh); border-radius: 4px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.10); overflow: hidden; }
  .fl .h44 { height: 44px; } .fl .h280 { height: 280px; } .fl .h430 { height: 430px; }
  .fl .cardin { padding: 13px 15px; }
  .fl .stwhy { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ii); margin: 9px 0 0; line-height: 1.45; }

  .fl .marker { height: 100%; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; padding: 0 14px; }
  .fl .mtitle { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--mm); }
  .fl .mprog { font-size: 12px; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .mtick { margin-left: auto; font-family: var(--mo); color: var(--mm); }

  .fl .phead { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--mm); margin: 0 0 10px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .fl .clock { margin-left: auto; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .x { color: var(--mm); font-size: 14px; }
  .fl .prests { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--mm); margin: 12px 0 5px; }
  .fl .prests:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .fl .pclaim { font-size: 13px; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .pconc { font-size: 13px; margin: 0; line-height: 1.45; }
  .fl .pwait { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; color: var(--mm); margin: 14px 0 0; }
  .fl .handoff { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 11px; color: var(--is); margin: 14px 0 0; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); }

  .fl .stance { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; margin: 10px 0 3px; display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: baseline; }
  .fl .stance.contests { color: var(--ox); font-weight: 700; }
  .fl .stance.supports { color: var(--mm); }
  .fl .who { font-family: var(--sf); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--ii); font-weight: 400; }
  .fl .quote { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; margin: 0; border-left: 2px solid var(--hh); padding-left: 8px; }

  /* hosted page */
  .fl .hosted { flex: 1; background: var(--pp); padding: 22px 30px; }
  .fl .hkick { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--mm); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .fl .htitle { font-size: 22px; color: var(--is); margin: 0 0 8px; line-height: 1.2; }
  .fl .hconc { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 16px; max-width: 40rem; }
  .fl .hgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 26px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); padding-top: 14px; }
  .fl .hfoot { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; color: var(--mm); margin: 14px 0 0; }

  .fl .spec { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 12px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); }
  .fl .spec div { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .fl .spec b { display: block; font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mm); font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 3px; }

  /* preference */
  .fl .prefwrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 320px 1fr; gap: 30px; align-items: start; }
  .fl .prefs { background: var(--ss); border: 1px solid var(--hh); border-radius: 4px; padding: 16px 18px; }
  .fl .pgroup { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--mm); margin: 0 0 9px; }
  .fl .pgroup + .opt { margin-top: 0; }
  .fl .prefs .pgroup:not(:first-child) { margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); }
  .fl .opt { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 16px 1fr; gap: 4px 9px; margin-bottom: 11px; align-items: start; }
  .fl .radio { width: 11px; height: 11px; border: 1px solid var(--mm); border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 4px; }
  .fl .opt.on .radio { border-color: var(--is); border-width: 4px; }
  .fl .opt b { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .opt.on b { font-weight: 700; }
  .fl .opt span:last-child { grid-column: 2; font-size: 12px; color: var(--mm); line-height: 1.35; }
  .fl .prefnote p { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.5; }

  /* measured curve */
  /* Budget ascends downward, so the reader travels the same direction the
     spending does and the fall-off after 512 is a shape rather than a number. */
  .fl .chart { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-top: 1px solid var(--hh); padding-top: 4px; }
  .fl .crow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 76px 1fr 58px 78px 68px; gap: 12px; align-items: center; padding: 7px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hh); }
  .fl .crow.head { padding: 0 0 8px; }
  .fl .crow.head div { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mm); }
  .fl .cbud { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 14px; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .cbud span { display: block; font-size: 9px; color: var(--mm); letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .fl .cbar { position: relative; height: 20px; background: #EDEEEA; }
  .fl .cfill { height: 100%; background: #C6CBC4; }
  .fl .crow.chosen .cfill { background: var(--ox); }
  .fl .cval { position: absolute; left: 8px; top: 1px; font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 12px; color: var(--is); }
  .fl .crow.chosen .cval { color: #fff; }
  .fl .csec, .fl .ccost { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 12px; color: var(--ii); }
  .fl .cmark { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--ox); font-weight: 700; }

  .fl .tbl { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 22px; }
  .fl .tbl th { font-family: var(--mo); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mm); font-weight: 400; text-align: left; padding: 0 14px 7px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hh); }
  .fl .tbl td { font-size: 14px; padding: 9px 14px 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hh); vertical-align: top; }
  .fl .tbl td:first-child { color: var(--mm); }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .fl .states, .fl .spec, .fl .hgrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .fl .prefwrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    /* The card heights stay real. They stack rather than sit side by side, but
       shrinking them to fit would delete the one thing they are here to show. */
    .fl .win { overflow-x: auto; }
